{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1476097-what-would-the-ravnos-bane-be-in-the-middle-ages","id":1476097,"title":"What would the Ravnos bane be in the Middle Ages?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-03-09T09:11:39-08:00","id":1476097,"title":"What would the Ravnos bane be in the Middle Ages?","content":"I am a huge fan of Vampire; the Dark Ages and I recently began considering if it could be played with 5e rules. One of the things I read was the V5 Companion and their Bane is the result of their Antediluvian's death.<br /> <br /> So, what Bane should we give them in the Middle Ages, when trying to get away from the whole unfortunate&quot;Gypsy criminal&quot; offensive stereotype?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer and Storyteller's Vault contributor. Find my work here: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/index.php?affiliate_id=17903\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.storytellersvault.com/ind...liate_id=17903</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1535-jackob","name":"Jackob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1535_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-09T10:06:47-08:00","id":1476101,"title":"","content":"Just take the normal Dark Ages bane (which is actually much better, they CAN do virtuous things, as it's built around defining a 'key trait' that they have, which doesn't have to be vice-fueled), and make it require a Resolve + Composure test with a Difficulty equal to 1 or 2 plus the Bane Severity (so default 3 or 4 Difficulty) rather than the roll from the DA book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-09T10:24:37-08:00","id":1476106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1476097-what-would-the-ravnos-bane-be-in-the-middle-ages?p=1476101#post1476101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just take the normal Dark Ages bane (which is actually much better, they CAN do virtuous things, as it's built around defining a 'key trait' that they have, which doesn't have to be vice-fueled), and make it require a Resolve + Composure test with a Difficulty equal to 1 or 2 plus the Bane Severity (so default 3 or 4 Difficulty) rather than the roll from the DA book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do this, but the difficulty to resist is a straight bane severity. Difficulty is significantly harder to achieve in v5 then in v20. If you play by RAW, v5 will have your players fail a significant amount of their checks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-09T11:06:02-08:00","id":1476108,"title":"","content":"Change it from Health to Willpower damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}